  <div class="pl-cards">
    <details class="pl-card-d">
      <summary>ArticleDetailViewModel.kt — nested combine() drops 9 unchecked casts (quality-4)</summary>
      <div class="pl-card">
        <p>Two private data classes (<code>ArticleGroup</code>, <code>ArchiveGroup</code>) split the 9 flows into typed groups of 4 and 5. The outer <code>combine(articleGroupFlow, archiveGroupFlow)</code> then produces <code>ArticleDetailState</code> with no casts. The <code>stateIn(WhileSubscribed(5000), viewModelScope)</code> call is preserved unchanged.</p>
        <!-- @include diff-block { "lines": [
          { "kind": "rem", "text": "combine(_article, _selectedTabIndex, …, _selectedArchiveContent) { values ->" },
          { "kind": "rem", "text": "    @Suppress(\"UNCHECKED_CAST\")" },
          { "kind": "rem", "text": "    ArticleDetailState(article = values[0] as Article?, …)" },
          { "kind": "add", "text": "private val articleGroupFlow = combine(_article, _selectedTabIndex, useFreediumFlow, _isLoading) { article, tab, useFreedium, loading ->" },
          { "kind": "add", "text": "    ArticleGroup(article, tab, useFreedium, loading)" },
          { "kind": "add", "text": "}" },
          { "kind": "add", "text": "private val archiveGroupFlow = combine(_remoteArchives, _localArchives, _archiveSyncing, _textSource, _selectedArchiveContent) { remote, local, syncing, textSrc, sel ->" },
          { "kind": "add", "text": "    ArchiveGroup(remote, local, syncing, textSrc, sel)" },
          { "kind": "add", "text": "}" },
          { "kind": "add", "text": "private val _state = combine(articleGroupFlow, archiveGroupFlow) { ag, arc ->" },
          { "kind": "add", "text": "    ArticleDetailState(article = ag.article, selectedTabIndex = ag.selectedTabIndex, …)" },
          { "kind": "ctx", "text": "}.stateIn(viewModelScope, SharingStarted.WhileSubscribed(5000), …) // unchanged" }
        ] } -->
      </div>
    </details>
    <details class="pl-card-d">
      <summary>ArticleDetailViewModel.kt — typed settings key (quality-6) + UrlModifier injection (reuse-5)</summary>
      <div class="pl-card">
        <p>All three <code>"USE_FREEDIUM"</code> string literals replaced with <code>SettingsPreferenceKeys.USE_FREEDIUM</code>. The three <code>val modifier = UrlModifier()</code> local allocations are removed; <code>urlModifier</code> is injected as a constructor parameter (Hilt provides the <code>@Singleton</code> instance from <code>UrlModifier.kt</code>).</p>
        <!-- @include diff-block { "lines": [
          { "kind": "rem", "text": ".filter { it == \"USE_FREEDIUM\" }" },
          { "kind": "add", "text": ".filter { it == SettingsPreferenceKeys.USE_FREEDIUM }" },
          { "kind": "rem", "text": "sharedPreferencesManager.getBoolean(\"USE_FREEDIUM\")" },
          { "kind": "add", "text": "sharedPreferencesManager.getBoolean(SettingsPreferenceKeys.USE_FREEDIUM)" },
          { "kind": "rem", "text": "val modifier = UrlModifier()  // ×3 across getArticle/autoPopulateText/loadArchiveContent" },
          { "kind": "add", "text": "// constructor: private val urlModifier: UrlModifier (injected @Singleton)" },
          { "kind": "add", "text": "modifier.modifyUrl(…)  →  urlModifier.modifyUrl(…)" }
        ] } -->
      </div>
    </details>
    <details class="pl-card-d">
      <summary>ArticleDetailViewModel.kt — ArchiveType enum constants replace magic strings (reuse-11)</summary>
      <div class="pl-card">
        <p>In <code>autoPopulateText()</code>, the hardcoded <code>"readability"</code> and <code>"markdown"</code> keys are replaced with <code>ArchiveType.READABILITY.archiveKey</code> and <code>ArchiveType.MARKDOWN.archiveKey</code>. The <code>ArchiveType</code> import is already present.</p>
        <!-- @include diff-block { "lines": [
          { "kind": "rem", "text": "archives.firstOrNull { it.archiveKey == \"readability\" }" },
          { "kind": "add", "text": "archives.firstOrNull { it.archiveKey == ArchiveType.READABILITY.archiveKey }" },
          { "kind": "rem", "text": "?: archives.firstOrNull { it.archiveKey == \"markdown\" }" },
          { "kind": "add", "text": "?: archives.firstOrNull { it.archiveKey == ArchiveType.MARKDOWN.archiveKey }" }
        ] } -->
      </div>
    </details>
    <details class="pl-card-d">
      <summary>UrlModifier.kt — @Singleton annotation</summary>
      <div class="pl-card">
        <p><code>UrlModifier</code> holds only <code>val</code> compiled Regex fields — no per-instance mutable state. Adding <code>@Singleton</code> allows Hilt to provide a single shared instance. No DI module needed if the class already has <code>@Inject constructor</code>.</p>
        <!-- @include diff-block { "lines": [
          { "kind": "rem", "text": "class UrlModifier {" },
          { "kind": "add", "text": "@Singleton" },
          { "kind": "add", "text": "class UrlModifier @Inject constructor() {" }
        ] } -->
      </div>
    </details>
    <details class="pl-card-d">
